notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

The Microsoft Security Response Center, MSRC, published the January disclosure and the March update covering source code and internal systems. Microsoft Security published guidance for responders. The MITRE page defines T1110.003, Password Spraying, the technique behind stage 01.

The background slides name their own sources: the csoh.org glossary, Microsoft Learn and MITRE ATT&CK.

== Related kill chains
layout: links
link: Vercel / Context.ai | breaches/vercel-context-ai-oauth.html
